  "notes": "This is a ずる-verb (a variant of する-verbs). Common conjugation uses {乗|じょう}じる (ichidan) rather than {乗|じょう}ずる:\n- {乗|じょう}じる・{乗|じょう}じます\n- て-form: {乗|じょう}じて\n- た-form: {乗|じょう}じた\n\nPATTERN (sense 1):\n～に{乗|じょう}じて (taking advantage of ~)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {隙|すき}に{乗|じょう}じる (to take advantage of an opening)\n- {混乱|こんらん}に{乗|じょう}じる (to exploit confusion)\n- {機|き}に{乗|じょう}じる (to seize the opportunity)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS (sense 1):\n- {付|つ}け{込|こ}む: To take advantage of — implies exploiting a weakness in a more calculated way.\n- {便乗|びんじょう}する: To take advantage of, to ride on — often implies riding on someone else's success or a trend.",
